44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=dynamicLighting kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=90 triangles=86403 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant, not a material key: the pixel shader replaces the lightmap-only factor with 0.62+0.38*dot(normal, lightDirection) for 90 visible materials / 86403 visible triangles; no VMT declares it, so every surface is shaded by the same guessed direction and the baked lightmap's own direct light is counted twice; off
44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=specular kind=pass-switch state=disabled declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=90 triangles=86403 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=a pass constant: one lobe (boost 0.12, exponent 32) for 90 visible materials / 86403 visible triangles; no visible material declares $phong, so the lobe is added to materials that never asked for one; off
44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=bump kind=pass-switch state=refused declared=25 visible=25 resolved=25 missing=0 materials=25 triangles=14710 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=METAL/METALDOOR001 resource=materials/Metal/metaldoor001_normal.vtf reason=off: the world pass has one bump sampler slot (--world-bump) and the per-material path is off too (--world-material-bump), so the 25 visible materials that name one of 17 distinct $bumpmap textures are drawn with no normal map at all
44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=$bumpmap2 kind=material-key state=not-declared declared=0 visible=0 resolved=0 missing=0 materials=0 triangles=0 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=0 first=- resource=- reason=no material declares $bumpmap2
44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=%detailtype kind=material-key state=refused declared=19 visible=19 resolved=0 missing=19 materials=19 triangles=49660 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=WOOD/WOOD_FLOOR002 resource=materials/overlays/detail006.vmt reason=detail layers are the --world-detail switch: the detail material's $basetexture is sampled at the atlas uv scaled by $detailscale and combined with the albedo by $detailblendmode; with the switch off the layer is refused; 19 of 19 referenced detail VMTs are absent from this install, so the layer's own texture and blend mode cannot be resolved here; %detailtype is a key in the material that names the layer, not in the detail VMT, and is read above; 3 materials name a %detailtype group (first=tf_bagel_grass); %detailtype names a detail-prop group that VBSP consumes at map compile time (it emits prop_detail sprites and models there), so the key never reaches a runtime shader and has no consumer here
44161.4 gpu: world lighting-control control=$ssbump kind=material-key state=refused declared=17 visible=17 resolved=11 missing=6 materials=17 triangles=7172 requested=0 effective=0 parsed=1 first=WINTER/BLENDGRAVELTOGRASS_BAGEL resource=Metal/wall011d_bump-ssbump reason=$ssbump selects `BUMPMAP == 2`, where the texel is not a signed normal but three bumpBasis weights against three lightmap directions; this pass samples one lightmap and one tangent-space normal, so these materials are refused by name even when --world-material-bump is on
